cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Monte-Neo in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Monte-Neo: an independent verifier for trading-strategy backtests"
abstract: >-
  Monte-Neo checks trading-strategy backtests written by AI coding agents and humans.
  It detects look-ahead bias with truncation and future-perturbation probes and a static
  lint, prices trading costs and execution delay, and deflates the Sharpe ratio by the number
  of variants tried. It returns a reproducible, optionally signed strategy-verdict/1
  certificate, and ships an MCP server for coding agents.
authors:
  - name: "NeoZorK"
    website: "https://github.com/NeoZorK"
version: "0.28.0"
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NeoZorK/Monte-Neo"
url: "https://neozork.github.io/Monte-Neo/"
keywords:
  - backtesting
  - look-ahead bias
  - overfitting
  - deflated Sharpe ratio
  - algorithmic trading
  - AI agents
  - Model Context Protocol
